{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Morning. Sit yourself down. What's the problem.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, it's my jaw. It hurts when I chew, and it clicks. Been getting on my nerves.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Three weeks. Ever since her sister's wedding.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): No, not three weeks. A fortnight. Well, actually a tiny bit before the wedding, a couple of days, but not three weeks. He always rounds up.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): So roughly two to three weeks. Left or right.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Left side. Just in front of the ear. It pops when I open wide.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Worse with stress.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): God, yes. I'm a bookkeeper and the year-end has been awful, I'm clenching at the desk all day. He says I grind my teeth in my sleep as well.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She does. Every night. Sounds like she's chewing gravel. Wakes me up.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't grind every night, that's the thing. Umm, maybe a couple of times a week if he's right, I wouldn't know, I'm asleep. I do wake up with sore teeth some mornings, I'll give him that.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever. I feel fine otherwise.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Chest, tummy, waterworks, all fine.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, all of that is fine. Nothing going on there.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Sorry, can I just say, yesterday was a washout. We were taking the grandson to the cricket and the weather was filthy, absolute downpour, his little shirt soaked before we got through the gate. Ended up in a cafe watching the highlights. He was still doing the commentary in the car this morning.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He did the six over the stand. Twice.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): He's only seven and he knows all the bowlers. Proper little commentator. Sorry, I'm wittering.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. Open, please. Tender over the left jaw joint, the click is there, no swelling, and the mouth opens fully.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any drug reactions I should know about.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Err, maybe. Years ago after a chest infection I came out in a rash and my lip went a bit puffy. They'd given me an antibiotic and a painkiller and nobody told me which. So maybe the antibiotic or the painkiller.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Still not sure which.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nobody wrote it down. I do take paracetamol though, two 500 milligram tablets when the jaw's bad, and that's been fine.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anything else regular.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Just that, now and then. Oh, and I stopped the ibruprofen last month, it was upsetting my stomach, not because of any rash.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): This is your jaw joint, from the clenching and the grinding. I won't be giving you any tablets for it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh good. I wasn't sure what I was allowed, after that business.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): Soft diet. Nothing chewy, no crusty bread, cut things small. And a soft mouth guard at night, from the chemist or your dentist.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): A guard, right. He'll be thrilled, very romantic. Do I wear it every night.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yes, at night. If it's not settling in four weeks, come back and see me."
 ],
